- # `↯/s.123.2` — `Git.RefError`
+ # `↯/s.123.2` — `Git.RefError`

- Raised when a value is not a valid Git reference name.
+ Levée lorsqu'une valeur n'est pas un nom de référence Git valide.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- Octogenarian validates reference names against `git
- check-ref-format`'s rules. The constructor records the offending
- `value` and a `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `$value
+ Octogenarian valide les noms de références selon les règles de `git
+ check-ref-format`. Le constructeur consigne la `value` fautive et
+ une `reason: Reason` ; le message rendu est `$value

- is not a valid Git reference because $reason`.
+ is not a valid Git reference because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
+ column  Code

- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
+ column  Raison
+ column  Signification

- column  Message
+ column  Message

- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.123.2.1`  `LeadingOrTrailingDot`  A path segment of the reference starts or ends with `.`.  `[↯/s.123.2.1] .verona is not a valid Git reference because a path segment starts or ends with .`  Trim the leading or trailing dot from the segment.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.2`  `ReservedSuffix`  A path segment matches `*.lock`, a pattern which Git reserves for lock files.  `[↯/s.123.2.2] feature.lock is not a valid Git reference because a path segment ends with the reserved suffix .lock`  Choose a name which does not match `*.lock`.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.3`  `ReservedSequence`  The name contains `@{`, which Git reserves for reflog selectors (e.g. `HEAD@{1}`).  `[↯/s.123.2.3] verona@{capulet} is not a valid Git reference because the name contains the reserved sequence @{`  Remove or replace the `@{` sequence.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.4`  `DoubleDot`  The name contains `..`, which Git reserves for range selectors.  `[↯/s.123.2.4] verona..capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains ..`  Replace the `..` with a single `.` or another separator.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.5`  `EmptySegment`  The name contains an empty path segment — typically a leading, trailing, or doubled `/`.  `[↯/s.123.2.5] verona//capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains an empty path segment`  Remove the empty segment.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.6`  `InvalidCharacter`  The name contains a character Git forbids in references: any of `*`, `[`, `\`, ` `, `^`, `~`, `:`, or `?`.  `[↯/s.123.2.6] verona capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains a character forbidden by Git`  Replace the forbidden character with `-` or `_`.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.7`  `BadHash`  The value passed to `Git.Hash` was not a 40-character lowercase hexadecimal string.  `[↯/s.123.2.7] abc is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a 40-character hexadecimal hash`  Provide the full 40-character SHA-1 commit hash.
- row  `↯/s.123.2.8`  `BadRefspec`  The value passed to `Git.Refspec.parse` was not a refspec: it had more than one `:` separating source and destination.  `[↯/s.123.2.8] a:b:c is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a valid refspec`  Write the refspec as `source`, `source:destination` or `:destination`, with an optional leading `+`.
+ column  Résolution
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.1`  `LeadingOrTrailingDot`  Un segment de chemin de la référence commence ou se termine par `.`.  `[↯/s.123.2.1] .verona is not a valid Git reference because a path segment starts or ends with .`  Retirez le point initial ou final du segment.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.2`  `ReservedSuffix`  Un segment de chemin correspond à `*.lock`, un motif que Git réserve aux fichiers de verrou.  `[↯/s.123.2.2] feature.lock is not a valid Git reference because a path segment ends with the reserved suffix .lock`  Choisissez un nom qui ne correspond pas à `*.lock`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.3`  `ReservedSequence`  Le nom contient `@{`, que Git réserve aux sélecteurs de reflog (par exemple `HEAD@{1}`).  `[↯/s.123.2.3] verona@{capulet} is not a valid Git reference because the name contains the reserved sequence @{`  Supprimez ou remplacez la séquence `@{`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.4`  `DoubleDot`  Le nom contient `..`, que Git réserve aux sélecteurs d'intervalles.  `[↯/s.123.2.4] verona..capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains ..`  Remplacez `..` par un seul `.` ou par un autre séparateur.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.5`  `EmptySegment`  Le nom contient un segment de chemin vide — en général un `/` initial, final ou doublé.  `[↯/s.123.2.5] verona//capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains an empty path segment`  Supprimez le segment vide.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.6`  `InvalidCharacter`  Le nom contient un caractère que Git interdit dans les références : l'un de `*`, `[`, `\`, ` `, `^`, `~`, `:` ou `?`.  `[↯/s.123.2.6] verona capulet is not a valid Git reference because the name contains a character forbidden by Git`  Remplacez le caractère interdit par `-` ou `_`.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.7`  `BadHash`  La valeur passée à `Git.Hash` n'était pas une chaîne hexadécimale de 40 caractères en minuscules.  `[↯/s.123.2.7] abc is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a 40-character hexadecimal hash`  Fournissez le hash SHA-1 complet du commit, sur 40 caractères.
+ row  `↯/s.123.2.8`  `BadRefspec`  La valeur passée à `Git.Refspec.parse` n'était pas une refspec : elle comportait plus d'un `:` séparant la source et la destination.  `[↯/s.123.2.8] a:b:c is not a valid Git reference because the value is not a valid refspec`  Écrivez la refspec sous la forme `source`, `source:destination` ou `:destination`, avec un `+` initial facultatif.

- ```
